    CAR_LIGHT_HOT:'#ffd2d8',
    CAR_HIP:      '#2aa3c0',      // the flank between shoulder and sill
    CAR_SILL:     '#12596e',      // under the widest line, always in shade
    /* Distinct from BOTH the roof and the body, or from overhead it is
       just more of the same surface. Nearly white against the roof's mid
       cyan, over a near black gap. */
    /* 250 luminance, over the edge's 246, and the brightest pixel in the
       whole frame in four biomes. Rule two says the car is second to the
       edge and it was first. Same treatment as the trail: down, not off. */
    CAR_SPOILER:  '#d8f4fa',
    CAR_WING_GAP: '#03141b',
    CAR_RIM:      '#c4f2fa',      // was 246, level with the edge
    CAR_RIM_GLOW: '214,254,255',
    CAR_TYRE:     '#0a0f14',
    CAR_TYRE_TOP: '#182430',
    CAR_SHADOW:   'rgba(0,0,0,0.5)',
    /* THE UNLOCKABLE COSMETICS. Every one of these is an ALTERNATE for a
       part that is not doing the finding: the rims, the light bar, the
       panel seams and the cool end of the tyre marks.
  
       THE BODY IS NOT ON THIS LIST AND THE REASON IT IS NOT HAS CHANGED.
       This used to read "and never will be, because the body colour is
       derived from the biome at maximum hue separation and that is the
       whole reason the car stays findable against all twelve. A player may
       not override it."
  
       The body is no longer derived from anything. It is pinned in
       PALETTE_FIXED, and findability is carried by saturation and contrast
       against the void instead, measured at 12 of 12 rather than the 11 of
       12 the rotating body managed. So the argument that the body could
       never be a player's choice is spent: a fixed body IS available to
       unlock, in a way it genuinely was not before.
  
       IT IS STILL NOT ON THE LIST, because that is a design decision and
       not a consequence, and nobody has taken it. What would have to be
       shown first is that every offered body clears the same twelve biome
       table this one does, which is a harder bar than the rims had to
       clear: a rim is a few dozen pixels of trim and the body is the
       silhouette. Recorded here so the next session does not read the old
       paragraph and think the question is closed.
  
       THE RIMS AND THE SEAMS ARE IN COLOUR AND THE LIGHTS ARE NOT, AND
       THAT SPLIT IS NEW. This used to read "in COLOUR, not PALETTE_FIXED,
       so they turn with the world like every other part of the car. A rim
       that ignored the wheel would be the one object on screen that
       belongs to no biome." It still holds for the rims and the seams,
       which are trim. It does not hold for the LIGHTS: see PALETTE_FIXED,
       where the tail light colours and the car's own glow now sit,
       because the first player of the released game lost track of which
       car was his and belonging to no biome is exactly what fixes it.
  
       ALL HELD UNDER THE ROAD EDGE. CAR_RIM was already brought down once
       for being level with it, so its alternates start from that lesson
       rather than repeating it. */
